            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "COUNTRYHILLS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been making this salad for several years and it's always well received. I reduced the hot water to 1 cup, dissolve the jello and add 3/4 cup of the drained pineapple juice. I also add 1 tsp. lemon juice. The smaller amount of liquid makes the salad firmer as I usually pour it into a jello mold."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Emily Brown Long"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe! I left out the celery and added a small peeled apple instead. I find that it really helps if you use some of the excess pinapple juice in the blender with the cranberries first. I don't blend the oranges or apples. I agree with only using 1 cup of water, too. (you can also use strawberry gelatin mix) Everyone in my family LOVES this cranberry salad! Yummy!!!",
            "datePublished": "2005-11-23T07:25:03.840Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy! My whole family loved it. It is made easier with the use of mandarin oranges.",
            "datePublished": "2003-12-31T08:45:25.840Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Vicky Gunkel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was just the recipe I was looking for that my mom used to make. I left out the nuts and celery (kids) and added an apple to grind up in the food processor with cranberries and the orange. This is so easy to whip up as a side dish adn well recieved by my Christmas Eve guests. Thanks for a winner!",
            "datePublished": "2006-12-25T18:02:30.417Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for Christmas dinner, I was a little nervous of what the kids might think but they LOVED it, alongwith all the adults. I mixed the jello with the water last so it wouldn't sit. I also used cranberry raspberry jello. Very, very good!! =}",
            "datePublished": "2004-01-08T06:07:16.160Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Awesome! I got lots of compliments at Thanksgiving by people starting with, \"I don't normally like cranberry salad but this is really good, could you give me the recipe?\" I used sugar free raspberry jello and also 3/4 c of sugar instead to lighten it. Also only used 1 cup of hot water.",
            "datePublished": "2005-11-25T07:02:04.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Thanks for the easy recipe. I didn't drain the\r\npineapple as much as I probably should have. \r\nI'd reduce the hot water to 1 3/4 cup \r\nto make the jello a bit firmer. The family liked\r\nit -- it's a keeper and will make it again.",
            "datePublished": "2001-11-26T14:47:06.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Anya Borden"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This came to my family from my grandmother (though after her death, an aunt revealed that it had been HER family's recipe) - as Southerners, we prefer pecans to walnuts, cut the sugar down to 3/4 cup, and reserve the pineapple juice to use for its equivalent in water. Makes the gelatin much more flavorful -- we still prefer the cherry jello to the cranberry -- otherwise too tart. Makes a lovely molded presentation.",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-19T11:15:31.607Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WorthyPeel8388"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added 3/4 c pineapple juice instead of the second cup of hot water. Very bright and tangy fruit salad. Will make again!",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-28T22:07:34.123Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "m-m-good"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I took this to a postponed Thanksgiving yesterday. We had to travel nearly 100 miles, but it survived it beautifully. I used about 3/4 cup Sucralose(Safeway's fake sugar), three Clementines for the one orange, both walnuts and an apple, and a dark jello. I didn't have lemon, so I added about two tablespoons of lime juice. As others suggested, I cut down a lot on the water, and used the reserved pineapple juice as part of it. It was crunchy(celery, nuts, and apple) and delicious--not too sweet. It was photogenic, but I forgot to do that! We had so many delicious things that I think someone must have taken a picture. I left the leftovers with the hostess, but my daughter and I like it a lot, so I'm going to make us another one.",
            "datePublished": "2012-11-25T12:24:43.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jodeans receipes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used canned whole berry cranberry sauce and added a Cup of chopped celery. It was wonderful. People asked for the recipe. Will definitely make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-25T18:27:56.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FLDeb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was looking for a cranberry recipe that I could get my family to eat, this one so far has the most votes. I make it every holiday now, love it!",
            "datePublished": "2026-04-01T18:47:25.264Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "1"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jeff"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The.amount.of water is double the amount of water that should be used along with the moisture from all of the fruits. A 3 oz pack of jello uses 1 cup of boiling water. Along with the moisture from the fruits this makes it the correct looseness.",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-01T00:44:39.564Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LivelyCow1858"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved the flavors and sweetness of this. I also enjoyed the crunch from the nuts and celery. There is an enzyme in pineapple which stops gelatin from setting, so if you want a 'set' salad then you may have to remove the pineapple. As it was, I really liked the texture of this as a holiday side dish.",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-10T17:16:36.894Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tracey Shooke'"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I only use 1/3 cup of sugar, that's sweet enough for my family. Thank you, it's a winner each and every year... We make it for Christmas too!",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-29T20:21:23.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "UpbeatSole7349"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been looking for a recipe to recreate the recipe my late grandma made very year and this just about nailed it. It was a little watery so I loved the \"tweak\" with the pineapple juice and will try that next time (Dad just LOVED this this year - can't wait to see his reaction to the tweaked recipe :)",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-29T19:16:28.260Z"
          },
          {
